---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import BreedCatsList from '../../components/BreedCatsList.astro';

const traits = [
  ['Body', 'Strong, muscular and sturdy. The powerful hind legs are longer than the front ones, giving the back a slight forward slope.'],
  ['Tail', 'Well furred, can be knotty, curved or even kinked. Between 3 and 12 cm long: over 8 cm is considered a fault in show cats.'],
  ['Head', 'Broad, trapezoidal in shape, with full cheeks.'],
  ['Nose', 'Medium length, with no defined stop.'],
  ['Ears', 'Set high on the skull, medium-sized, generously furred.'],
  ['Coat', 'Comes in short-haired and semi-long varieties. In the semi-long variety, the coat is medium length, soft and silky, with little undercoat, longer on the ruff, belly and flanks.'],
];

const allowedColors = ['Black', 'Red', 'Tortoiseshell', 'Blue', 'Cream', 'Blue tortie', 'Silver', 'Smoke', 'White (patches)', 'Tabby'];
const excludedColors = ['Chocolate', 'Fawn', 'Cinnamon', 'Lavender', 'Colorpoint'];
---
<Layout
  title="Kurilian Bobtail"
  lang="en"
  description="Everything about the Kurilian Bobtail: history, temperament, appearance, recognized colors and our cats."
>
  <div class="breed-masthead profano">
    <span class="eyebrow">The profane</span>
    <h1>Kurilian Bobtail</h1>
    <div class="rule"></div>
  </div>

  <h2>History</h2>
  <p>
    The Kurilian is a recently recognized breed that developed naturally: it existed
    in total isolation for a long time on the Kuril Islands, an archipelago between
    Russia and Japan.
  </p>
  <p>
    Virtually unknown in the rest of the world, it became fairly popular in Russia
    thanks to its good temperament and wild look, despite lacking the kind of formal
    selective breeding that would classify it as a breed.
  </p>
  <p>
    Numerous accounts mention short-tailed cats brought home by military personnel
    and scientists stationed on those islands around the middle of the last century.
    A proper breeding and selection program only began in the late 1980s, started by
    two Russian breeders.
  </p>

  <h2>Temperament</h2>
  <p>
    The Kurilian's wild appearance doesn't reflect the breed's temperament. It's an
    intelligent, playful cat that enjoys the company of its owner and other pets, and
    adapts perfectly to apartment life. In the wild it's known for its skills as a
    hunter, fisher and swimmer - traits it keeps even as a house cat.
  </p>

  <h2>Appearance</h2>
  <dl class="traits-grid">
    {traits.map(([term, def]) => (
      <>
        <dt>{term}</dt>
        <dd>{def}</dd>
      </>
    ))}
  </dl>

  <h2>Recognized colors</h2>
  <p>
    The Kurilian is recognized in the traditional colors - black, red and
    tortoiseshell - along with their dilutions: blue, cream and blue tortie, with or
    without white patches. Silver and smoke variants are also allowed, in all colors,
    both solid and with tabby markings.
  </p>
  <div class="color-chips">
    {allowedColors.map((c) => <span class="chip allowed">{c}</span>)}
  </div>
  <p class="excluded-note">
    Since crossbreeding with other breeds isn't allowed for the Kurilian Bobtail,
    colors that betray obvious hybridization are excluded:
  </p>
  <div class="color-chips">
    {excludedColors.map((c) => <span class="chip excluded">{c}</span>)}
  </div>

  <h2>Registration</h2>
  <p>
    This breed still allows for "novice" registration: a cat can be submitted for
    recognition even without a pedigree proving its lineage, as long as its origin
    from the Kuril Islands is certified.
  </p>

  <h2>Our Kurilian Bobtail cats</h2>
  <BreedCatsList breed="Kurilian Bobtail" lang="en" />

  <p><a class="text-link" href="/en/litters">See our available litters →</a></p>
</Layout>

<style>
  .breed-masthead { margin-bottom: 1.75rem; }
  .breed-masthead .eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--profano);
  }
  .breed-masthead h1 {
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.75rem);
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .breed-masthead .rule {
    height: 3px;
    width: 6rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    background: repeating-linear-gradient(90deg, var(--profano) 0 10px, transparent 10px 16px);
  }
  .text-link { color: var(--profano); font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }
  .text-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  h2 { margin-top: 2.25rem; }

  .traits-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 9rem 1fr;
    gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
  .traits-grid dt {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--profano);
    padding-top: 0.15rem;
  }
  .traits-grid dd { margin: 0 0 0.5rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .traits-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .traits-grid dt { margin-top: 0.75rem; }
  }

  .color-chips { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; margin-top: 0.75rem; }
  .chip {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: 0.35rem 0.8rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    border: 1px solid;
  }
  .chip.allowed { color: var(--profano); border-color: var(--profano); background: var(--profano-soft); }
  .chip.excluded {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    border-color: var(--line);
    background: var(--paper-2);
    text-decoration: line-through;
    text-decoration-color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .excluded-note { margin-top: 1.5rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
</style>
